    "intro_narrative": "The year is 1892, and you find yourself locked in the subterranean workshop of the infamous Clockwork Baron. The air is thick with the smell of coal smoke and lubricating oil, and the constant hiss of steam pipes echoes through the dimly lit cavern. You were hired to retrieve the blueprints for a revolutionary perpetual motion engine, but the Baron's paranoia has led him to secure the exit behind a labyrinth of interconnected mechanical devices and analytical engines. Your only way out is to navigate this complex web of steampunk technology. You must power up the various difference engines, decipher punched card schematics, and align the heavy brass gears of the Baron's creations. The grand door that stands between you and freedom is controlled by a massive mechanical vault system. By logically tracing the flow of data through these roaring, steam-driven machines, you can bypass the security locks and escape before the Baron returns. Keep a close eye on how the devices connect to one another; every gear and pressure valve relies on another to function.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
